              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "TG Breath of Life; Man, a Spirit Child of Heavenly Father.",
            "prettyString": "TG Breath of Life; TG Man, a Spirit Child of Heavenly Father",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Breath of Life",
                "entryId": "tg-breath-of-life",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              },
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Man, a Spirit Child of Heavenly Father",
                "entryId": "tg-man-a-spirit-child-of-heavenly-father",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou canst answer me, set thy words in order before me, stand up.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I am according to thy wish in God’s stead: I also am formed out of the clay.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, my terror shall not make thee afraid, neither shall my hand be heavy upon thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Surely thou hast spoken in mine hearing, and I have heard the voice of thy words, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 74
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "I am clean without transgression, I am innocent; neither is there iniquity in me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, he findeth occasions against me, he counteth me for his enemy,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "He putteth my feet in the stocks, he marketh all my paths.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, in this thou art not just: I will answer thee, that God is greater than man.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "Isa. 55:9 (8–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Why dost thou strive against him? for he giveth not account of any of his matters.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "For God speaketh once, yea twice, yet man perceiveth it not.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "In a dream, in a vision of the night, when deep sleep falleth upon men, in slumberings upon the bed;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Dream."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Dream.",
            "prettyString": "TG Dream",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Dream",
                "entryId": "tg-dream",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Then he openeth the ears of men, and sealeth their instruction,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "That he may withdraw man from his purpose, and hide pride from man.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "He keepeth back his soul from the pit, and his life from perishing by the sword.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Hell."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Hell.",
            "prettyString": "TG Hell",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Hell",
                "entryId": "tg-hell",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "He is chastened also with pain upon his bed, and the multitude of his bones with strong pain:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "So that his life abhorreth bread, and his soul dainty meat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "His flesh is consumed away, that it cannot be seen; and his bones that were not seen stick out.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, his soul draweth near unto the grave, and his life to the destroyers.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "If there be a messenger with him, an interpreter, one among a thousand, to shew unto man his uprightness:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Then he is gracious unto him, and saith, Deliver him from going down to the pit: I have found a ransom.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "1 Tim. 2:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Tim. 2:6.",
            "prettyString": "1 Timothy 2:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1timothy",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 2,
                    "end": 2,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 6,
                        "end": 6
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "His flesh shall be fresher than a child’s: he shall return to the days of his youth:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 5:14."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Kgs. 5:14.",
            "prettyString": "2 Kings 5:14",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 5,
