        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "He looketh upon men, and if any say, I have sinned, and perverted that which was right, and it profited me not;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 31
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "He will deliver his soul from going into the pit, and his life shall see the light.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Lo, all these things worketh God oftentimes with man,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "To bring back his soul from the pit, to be enlightened with the light of the living.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "Mark well, O Job, hearken unto me: hold thy peace, and I will speak.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:31",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou hast any thing to say, answer me: speak, for I desire to justify thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 33:32",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 32
      },
